is orderable or active at an individual parcel."],[3,"General money-saving and contract guidance contains no parcel-level evidence of network coverage, line capability or measured speed."],[4,"Text-relay obligations and accessibility features do not demonstrate broadband availability, mobile signal or service performance at a parcel."],[5,"Emergency video relay availability is a national accessibility service and does not prove local connectivity or resilience at a specific parcel."],[6,"Disabled-user support rights and priority repair policies do not establish actual network technology, coverage or measured parcel performance."],[7,"Provider conduct rules and vulnerable-customer guidance are regulatory requirements, not evidence of service availability at an individual address."],[8,"Complaint and ADR procedures do not verify broadband orderability, mobile coverage, technology or measured speed at a parcel."],[9,"Automatic compensation rules and signatory participation do not prove that a service failure occurred or that connectivity exists at a specific parcel."],[10,"Contract-end notifications and best-deal reminders provide no evidence about parcel-level infrastructure, coverage or line performance."],[11,"Customer-service comparisons and corrected aggregate fault data cannot be promoted to exact parcel availability or measured speed."],[12,"Faster ADR access and inflation-linked compensation are consumer protections and contain no parcel-level connectivity evidence."],[13,"Upper 6 GHz authorisation and AFC sharing rules do not prove Wi-Fi or mobile deployment, coverage or capacity at a specific parcel."],[14,"Direct-to-Device exemption regulations authorise technical use but do not establish retail service, signal or availability at an individual parcel."],[15,"Mobile-terminal licence exemptions define legal equipment use and do not demonstrate network deployment, coverage or performance at a parcel."]],"source_count_inflation_prevented":true,"fake_data":false,